#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gf180mcu.atf -- DRAFT, hand-authored RedHawk Apache Technology File for
# GF180MCU (5LM+1TM stack, 11kA top metal), for use with `make rail` in
# synopsys_croc (rail.tech_file / RedHawk-SC Fusion).
#
# STATUS: first-pass draft, syntax UNVERIFIED against a real ATF spec (none
# was available locally or to the author at authoring time). Values are
# real, sourced from GF180MCU's own open-source PDK data; the surrounding
# ATF keyword/block syntax is a best-effort guess to be corrected by
# redhawk_sc's own parser errors and by human review before being trusted
# for any real signoff claim. Needs review -- see conversation/commit
# history for context before relying on this.
#
# All numeric values below are taken directly from:
#   ~/.ciel/ciel/gf180mcu/versions/<rev>/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/magic/gf180mcuD.tech
# (the open-source GF180MCU PDK's own Magic tech file, managed by ciel),
# specifically its "extract" section, which itself cites GlobalFoundries'
# published process documents:
#   - Resistance (resist/contact blocks):  180MCU_YI-141-EP059-01_10.pdf
#   - Capacitance (areacap/sidewall/etc.): PDS_035_03
# "typ" corner values used throughout (magic's variant() with no hrhc/lrhc
# suffix); hrhc/lrhc corner values are also present in the source .tech file
# if a corner-specific ATF is ever needed.
#
# Stack (from gf180mcuD.tech 'height' section, z0/thickness in um):
#   Metal1  z=1.23  t=0.55   Rs=90  mOhm/sq
#   Via1    z=1.78  t=0.60   R=4500 mOhm/via (via1 not separately listed in
#                              the contact block above metal2 -- see NOTE)
#   Metal2  z=2.38  t=0.55   Rs=90  mOhm/sq
#   Via2    z=2.93  t=0.60   R=4500 mOhm/via (m2c)
#   Metal3  z=3.53  t=0.55   Rs=90  mOhm/sq
#   Via3    z=4.08  t=0.60   R=4500 mOhm/via
#   Metal4  z=4.68  t=0.55   Rs=90  mOhm/sq
#   Via4    z=5.23  t=0.60   R=4500 mOhm/via
#   Metal5  z=5.83  t=1.0025 Rs=40  mOhm/sq   (thick top/RDL-like metal)
#
# NOTE: the source .tech file's 'contact' block lists m2c/m3c/via3/via4 all
# at 4500 mOhm -- it does not give a separately-named via1 resistance
# (likely because via1 sits between metal1/metal2 and isn't broken out
# under a different name in this deck). Reused the same 4500 mOhm value for
# via1 pending confirmation -- flag this specifically in review.
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

UNITS
    LENGTH   UM
    RESISTANCE OHM
    CAPACITANCE FF
END

LAYER Metal1
    TYPE       CONDUCTOR
    HEIGHT     1.23
    THICKNESS  0.55
    RPSQ       0.090
    AREA_CAP   0.029304
END

LAYER Via1
    TYPE       VIA
    FROM_LAYER Metal1
    TO_LAYER   Metal2
    HEIGHT     1.78
    THICKNESS  0.60
    RES        4.5
END

LAYER Metal2
    TYPE       CONDUCTOR
    HEIGHT     2.38
    THICKNESS  0.55
    RPSQ       0.090
    AREA_CAP   0.015016
END

LAYER Via2
    TYPE       VIA
    FROM_LAYER Metal2
    TO_LAYER   Metal3
    HEIGHT     2.93
    THICKNESS  0.60
    RES        4.5
END

LAYER Metal3
    TYPE       CONDUCTOR
    HEIGHT     3.53
    THICKNESS  0.55
    RPSQ       0.090
    AREA_CAP   0.010094
END

LAYER Via3
    TYPE       VIA
    FROM_LAYER Metal3
    TO_LAYER   Metal4
    HEIGHT     4.08
    THICKNESS  0.60
    RES        4.5
END

LAYER Metal4
    TYPE       CONDUCTOR
    HEIGHT     4.68
    THICKNESS  0.55
    RPSQ       0.090
    AREA_CAP   0.007602
END

LAYER Via4
    TYPE       VIA
    FROM_LAYER Metal4
    TO_LAYER   Metal5
    HEIGHT     5.23
    THICKNESS  0.60
    RES        4.5
END

LAYER Metal5
    TYPE       CONDUCTOR
    HEIGHT     5.83
    THICKNESS  1.0025
    RPSQ       0.040
    AREA_CAP   0.0
END
